
Build the executable: `make build`
	This requires GCC 5ish, Bison 3.0, sed, GNU M4.
        This produces the binary 'build/main'

Build the pdf: `make doc`
	This requires noweb and a LaTeX distribution.
        This produces the document 'writeup.pdf' formatted for binding.

Build both: `make all`

Remove all intermediates and outputs: `make clean`

Remove all source files as well: `make distclean`
	noweb will be required to extract them from the .nw documents.

`make V=1 [target]` to see verbose commands.
`make DEBUG=1 [target]` to set CFLAGS for debugging.
`make DOC=preview doc` for slightly nicer on-screen reading (perhaps).
